@baseUrl = https://localhost:7100
@email = synthetic-student@example.test
@password = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_DEMO_PASSWORD}}
@userToken = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_USER_TOKEN}}
@refreshToken = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_REFRESH_TOKEN}}
@challengeToken = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_CHALLENGE_TOKEN}}
@clientSecret = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_WORKLOAD_SECRET}}
@workloadToken = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_WORKLOAD_TOKEN}}
@identityId = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_IDENTITY_ID}}
@sessionId = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_SESSION_ID}}
@operationId = {{$processEnv VAIRAS_OPERATION_ID}}

### Register; returns 202 without exposing identity or email token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Request VerifyEmail or ResetPassword
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/challenges
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{email}}","purpose":"VerifyEmail"}

### Complete verification using the token obtained from the actual SMTP email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/challenges/completion
Content-Type: application/json

{"challengeToken":"{{challengeToken}}"}

### For ResetPassword add newPassword; this revokes all current sessions
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/challenges/completion
Content-Type: application/json

{"challengeToken":"{{challengeToken}}","newPassword":"{{password}}"}

### Password login requires completed email verification
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Rotate once; reuse of this token revokes its whole session family
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken":"{{refreshToken}}"}

### Reuse the same operation ID for an exact retry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/sessions/{{sessionId}}/revocation
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{operationId}}

### OAuth client credentials, never an end-user password grant
POST {{baseUrl}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=user-management&client_secret={{clientSecret}}&scope=identity.validate%20school.profile-provisioning%20confirmations.validate

### Service-to-service admission with separate workload audience and scope
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/v1/sessions/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{workloadToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"identityId":"{{identityId}}","sessionId":"{{sessionId}}"}

### Start an allowlisted OIDC login; retain its HttpOnly cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/oidc/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{"issuer":"https://YOUR_CONFIGURED_ISSUER","redirectUri":"https://YOUR_FRONTEND/oidc/callback","purpose":"Login"}

### Explicit linking additionally requires the existing active user session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/oidc/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"issuer":"https://YOUR_CONFIGURED_ISSUER","redirectUri":"https://YOUR_FRONTEND/oidc/callback","purpose":"Link"}

### Browser frontend forwards code/state and the server-set cookie after provider redirect
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/oidc/callback
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"{{$processEnv VAIRAS_OIDC_CODE}}","state":"{{$processEnv VAIRAS_OIDC_STATE}}"}

### Public issuer metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### Public signing material only
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### Process and owned-resource probes
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Database, signing keys and protection availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Negative example: empty identity binding must return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/v1/sessions/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{workloadToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"identityId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","sessionId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"}
